:: chowkidar_d3
Ramesh sits in his booth like a sentry whose war ended thirty years ago. Newspaper folded to the crossword. Thermos. Transistor radio murmuring Marathi news.

He looks up. His eyes do the automated scan of a face that passes him four times a day.

<div class="dialogue">"Good morning, Kavya didi."<span class="gloss-en">Good morning, sister Kavya.</span></div>

Your heart   Kavya's heart, faster RPM   lurches. He said the name. Her name. At you. And his face shows nothing. No squint, no double-take. You're Kavya to him. The disguise is the body itself.

"Good morning," you manage. The vocal cords do the work   the pitch correct, the Tamil undertone in place, the body performing even while the mind screams.

He returns to seven across. You're past.
<<run setup.flag("chowkidar_passed")>>
<<hubreturn>>


